* mkdir = make directory(folder).
  - creates a new folder.

  - EX: mkdir test

* pwd = print working directory

* ls = list everything in current working directory.

* cd = change directory
  - EX: cd test

* cd .. = go out of folder.
  - .. = the outer folder.

* NodeJS = free, open-source, cross-paltform JavaScript runtime environment that lets devs create servers. web apps, command line tools and scripts.

* node = cmd that lets us run JavaScript code outside of a browser.
  - EX: node react-basics.js

* npm = node package manager
  - package = external library

  - cmd that lets us install external libraries or packages into our project.

  - EX: npm install supersimpledev

* Some packagaes add a command to our command line.
  - EX: "create-vite" package adds the "create-vite" cmd.

  - "create-vite": cmd helps us set up a new React project.

* npx = cmd that installs the package AND runs the cmd in the command line.
  - 'x' = execute

  - EX: npx create-vite

  - @ means using a specific version of "create-vite"

  - EX: npx create-vite@6.5.0

* Run "npm install"
  - Inside the newly created "chatbot-project", we hae a file called "package.json" which contains l of all packages and dependencies needed for project.

  - "npm install" will install all these packages.

  - All packages will be downloaded into "node_modules" folder.

* Run "npm run dev"
  - This will start up our new React website.

* "src" = source folder that contains code for our website.
  - JS, CSS, etc

* "public" = folder that contains files that should be available to the public. We can access these using a URL.
  - EX: Given an image URL, we can access it.

* "eslint.config.js" = using by eslint.

* eslint = highlights problems in our JavaScript code.
  - Install the extension on VSCode to use.

* "index.html" = contains HTML code for project.

* "package-lock.json" = saves the package version numbers of all the packages we install.
  - This makes sure we get the same versions for all these packages.

  - npm AUTOMATICALLY updates "package-lock.json", so we do not need to update it.

* "package.json" = contains list of packages we need for the project.

* "vite.config.js" = configures Vite(tool we used to set u project, build the website, and create server).
  - A server puts our website at a URL.

* "main.jsx" renders the "App" component.
  - It wraps the "App" component in a "StrictMode".

* "<StrictMode>" = gives us some additional checks and warnings when developing our app.

* Best practice is to separate each component into its own file.

* "rmdir" removes a directory.
  - EX: rmdir test2

